?\n[S25T11] (dia_id: D25:11)\n\nCalvin: Yeah, it's a way for me to express myself and work through my emotions. It's like my own form of therapy.\n[S25T12] (dia_id: D25:12)\n\nDave: Yeah, I get it. Cars give me an outlet to express myself. It's like a little oasis of calm. Whenever I'm working on one, it's like I'm connecting back with myself. And yeah, the music helps too! Look at my garage, a little dirty, but everything is in its place.\n[Image caption: a photography of a garage with a bunch of tools hanging on the wall]\n[S25T13] (dia_id: D25:13)\n\nCalvin: Looking cool - what made you start working on cars?\n[S25T14] (dia_id: D25:14)\n\nDave: Ever since I was ten, I've been fascinated with how machines work. I found an old car in a neighbor's garage and asked if I could fix it. That's when my love for car engineering began! I enjoyed transforming it from broken-down to high-running, and that sense of accomplishment made me hooked—so I've been working on cars ever since.\n[Image caption: a photo of a man working on a car in a garage]\n[S25T15] (dia_id: D25:15)\n\nCalvin: Impressive! That must have taken a lot of skill and determination to bring that car back to life. Was it a classic car? Do you still have it or are you currently working on another project?\n[S25T16] (dia_id: D25:16)\n\nDave: Thanks Calvin! It was a fun project. I restored a car last year, but I sold it to a collector. Now I'm working on something new, and it's quite a challenge! Take a look at this wonderful car!\n[Image caption: a photo of a black car parked in a parking lot]\n[S25T17] (dia_id: D25:17)\n\nCalvin: Cool! Been wanting to try that. What would you say is the toughest part of car restoration?\n[S25T18] (dia_id: D25:18)\n\nDave: It takes a lot of patience, but the payoff is worth it. Paying extra attention to detail isn't easy, but it pays off.\n[S25T19] (dia_id: D25:19)\n\nCalvin: Yeah, details can really make a difference. It's what makes something great, like a well-crafted rap song or a sleek and stylish car.\n[S25T20] (dia_id: D25:20)","text_sha256":"6172efe69e75d92e6ff9c4b88fbbd1c9217f062cd6b7ea1295e9b2a267cd843f","timestamp":"2023-10-23T14:17:00"},{"attribution_index_sha256":"08302ae53c7681312a62f5734d6ef73dfd8c86405ba319838bd79230cce094d2","attribution_units":[{"dia_ids":["D14:7"],"kind":"raw_turn","line_end":31,"line_start":30,"source_locators":["[S14T7]"],"text_sha256":"e5b679dbac67112047fa5a6198b2ac52627b561adec187f16168653099b0c663"},{"dia_ids":["D14:8"],"kind":"raw_turn","line_end":35,"line_start":33,"source_locators":["[S14T8]"],"text_sha256":"4a14aff654da4dba41fe04c0453717c2ffee2813be3277018669350423d0ad32"},{"dia_ids":["D14:9"],"kind":"raw_turn","line_end":38,"line_start":37,"source_locators":["[S14T9]"],"text_sha256":"fb8c33ba7839c00cf3f3f4bc342cd71d81942147ac15cc867c08d4a5d3f8a460"},{"dia_ids":["D14:10"],"kind":"raw_turn","line_end":41,"line_start":40,"source_locators":["[S14T10]"],"text_sha256":"56a68406d8f3cb59ed614112fee7ac1a3e483b145c11810aebb5817a715ecb43"},{"dia_ids":["D14:11"],"kind":"raw_turn","line_end":45,"line_start":43,"source_locators":["[S14T11]"],"text_sha256":"e05b1966db455d34b12ba4c5521e8d10cac4a8b2ee5308b244125f3175c69f4f"},{"dia_ids":["D14:12"],"kind":"raw_turn","line_end":48,"line_start":47,"source_locators":["[S14T12]"],"text_sha256":"357d8d86869eeef4218bd25b7b1960adf692f46deb54ba1a7fc56af1d90b115a"},{"dia_ids":["D14:13"],"kind":"raw_turn","line_end":51,"line_start":50,"source_locators":["[S14T13]"],"text_sha256":"481eaa089e39487a40b7aee31de9c089c29a8cf3b667271c7b0bc653c3c0cbd6"},{"dia_ids":["D14:14"],"kind":"raw_turn","line_end":54,"line_start":53,"source_locators":["[S14T14]"],"text_sha256":"76aba909aeb7a3a47c2dc26db3e8f01f2aa3a81a7ec6ef116358120bde5f69ed"},{"dia_ids":["D14:15"],"kind":"raw_turn","line_end":57,"line_start":56,"source_locators":["[S14T15]"],"text_sha256":"7ef3ac279271d35edac5491ae9eb31faf6e6e9854364e15b33823c331c21ebd8"},{"dia_ids":["D14:16"],"kind":"raw_turn","line_end":60,"line_start":5